<%# One entry of a conversation that has already been read: the reader's own
    prompt, or a turn that is over.

    Its own partial because the page is not always painted from the whole
    transcript: a turn that arrives while the reader is looking — a batch of sub
    agents reporting back — is appended to the page as it stands. What is
    appended has to be what a reload would draw, or the same conversation would
    look different depending on how the reader got to it. -%>
<% if entry[:kind] == :prompt -%>
<%= View.render("_message", role: "user", text: entry[:text], anchor: "m-#{entry[:idx]}",
                            landed: landed) %>
<% else -%>
<div class="turn is-done<%= " is-landed" if landed %>"<% if entry[:idx] %> id="m-<%= entry[:idx] %>"<% end %>>
  <%= View.render("_report_sep") if entry[:report] -%>
  <div class="turn-body"><%= View.render("_timeline", items: entry[:items],
                                          token_query: token_query,
                                          ig_accounts: ig_accounts,
                                          ig_linkable_accounts: ig_linkable_accounts,
                                          ig_persona: ig_persona) %></div>
</div>
<% end -%>
